<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Braulio Carrillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800–1845</span> · Also known as Braulio Carrillo Colina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Braulio Carrillo was head of state of Costa Rica from 1835 to 1837 and again from 1838 to 1842. He defeated the rival towns of Cartago, Heredia and Alajuela in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league">War of the League</a> in 1835, fixed the capital at San José, encouraged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> growing and reformed the law. In 1838 he took Costa Rica out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/braulio-carrillo.jpg" alt="Braulio Carrillo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos Sanabria Gonzalez · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braulio_Carrillo_Colina_Retrato.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
